'''''Erodium ciconium''''', the '''common stork's bill''', is a species of annual herb in the family [[Geraniaceae]]. They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 21&nbsp;cm tall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Erodium ciconium (L.) L'Hér. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/595136|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mifsud|first=Stephen|date=2002-08-23|title=Erodium ciconium (Sand Storkbill) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands.|url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/GERN/Erodium_ciconium.php|access-date=2022-02-16|website=www.maltawildplants.com|language=en-us}}</ref>

